<title>DENMARK: Phoenix reticent on Superfos bid.</title>
<headline>Phoenix reticent on Superfos bid.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish roadbuilder Phoenix Contractors had little to say on Friday about a fresh bid by construction and chemicals group Superfos, other than to say that it was not significantly higher than a rival offer from Norway's Rieber &amp; Son.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not so much more than Rieber has offered. (But) My immediate reaction is that Superfos now has the highest bid,&quot; Phoenix chairman Henry Petersen told Reuters.</p>
<p>Superfos earlier increased an earlier offer to 730 Danish crowns per A-share and 655 crowns per B-share, trumping Rieber's 725 crowns per A-share and 650 crowns per C-share.</p>
</text>
